  "query_preview": "(This evening through Friday)...\nIssued at 211 PM EDT Fri Aug 28 2026\n\nRest of This Afternoon through Saturday...\n\nQuiet weather will continue this period. High pressure will be at \nthe surface. The few to scattered cumulus will dissipate early this \nevening. Upper energy will bring some high clouds tonight through \nSaturday. \n\nThere may be some patchy fog tonight depending on how thick the \ncirrus becomes. Guidance looks a bit warm for low temperatures \nagain, so nudged them down a bit. Lows will be in the upper 50s to \nlower 60s. Highs on Saturday will generally be in the lower to \nmiddle 80s.\n\nSaturday night through Sunday night...\n\nAn 850mb jet will aid in maintaining convection as it moves into the \nGreat Lakes region Saturday night. This convection will ride around \nthe upper high (the high will be to the southwest of central \nIndiana). While some models like the NAM try to bring some of this \ninto parts of the area later Saturday night into Sunday, believe \nthat the ridge will win prevail across central Indiana and keep the \narea dry. Will continue with a dry forecast.\n\nWarmer air will start to move into the area as the ridge builds on \nSunday, with highs in the upper 80s to lower 90s expected. Southwest \nsurface winds will bring in more humid air as well.\n\nMonday and beyond...\n\nThe upper ridge will keep convection at bay at least through \nTuesday. It may weaken enough for isolated convection to pop up \nWednesday through Friday afternoons, but confidence remains low.\n\nThe main story will be heat with highs in the 90s each day. Low \ntemperatures mainly in the 70s won't provide much relief. Humid air \nwill provide heat indices near 100 degrees for at least Tuesday into \nThursday. These conditions will likely require a Heat Advisory due \nto the length of the heat.",
